bility, distribution control and monetisation stability, and capability gaps in adopting AI, automation and advanced analytics. Mitigated through intelligent automation, strengthening owned-and-operated platforms, and upskilling in AI and data.","risk":"Technology and innovation risk (AI-driven, platform-centric media)"},{"note":"Risk of financial loss or disruption of operations from failure of IT systems, hackers gaining access to the website/platforms or sensitive data, and virus/malware/ransomware attacks; a data-security lapse could impact stakeholder trust, disrupt operations and cause regulatory or reputational consequences. Mitigated by ISO 27001 certification, Zero Trust architecture, encryption, backups, periodic vulnerability assessments, multiple security controls and a cyber insurance policy.","risk":"Cybersecurity and data privacy"},{"note":"Any default may attract penal provisions and impact the Company's reputation, and the Company may face litigation from third parties by virtue of being in the news industry. Mitigated through a compliance monitoring system, in-house legal experts and external consultation, and continuous monitoring of regulatory changes.","risk":"Regulatory, compliance and litigation risk"},{"note":"BRSR material-issue table records that the fast-paced nature of the media industry exposes the workforce to significant health and safety risks, with negative financial implications; mitigated by group insurance, an in-house medical facility, hospital partnerships, wellness workshops and PPE.","risk":"Health, safety and employee well-being"},{"note":"Climate change may increase the frequency and severity of natural disasters, and companies with major/key operations concentrated at one place are at risk; mitigated by analysing disaster impact, planning protective measures and maintaining adequate insurance coverage.","risk":"Loss of assets or profit due to natural calamities and operational concentration"}],"rpt":{},"rpt_date":"","s":"TV